this gBASIC reads comments: true
opened, the caret on line 1, in the first run: doc-5@5 markdown, doc-10@10 markdown; folds 5-6
the caret on code, line 8: doc-1@1 markdown, doc-5@5 markdown, doc-10@10 markdown; folds 1-3, 5-6
  the text is untouched: true, unsaved: false
the caret into the second run: doc-1@1 markdown, doc-10@10 markdown; folds 1-3
a click on the first run's prose
  the caret is on line 1: doc-5@5 markdown, doc-10@10 markdown; folds 5-6
the collapse control on prose
  pressed once: block-collapsed -> doc-1@1 markdown, doc-5@5 markdown collapsed, doc-10@10 markdown; folds 1-3, 5-6
  pressed again: block-expanded -> doc-1@1 markdown, doc-5@5 markdown, doc-10@10 markdown; folds 1-3, 5-6
a paragraph typed at the top, as the editor would: the prose moves with its lines
  doc-1@1 markdown, doc-3@3 markdown, doc-7@7 markdown, doc-12@12 markdown; folds 3-5, 7-8
Settings > Show documentation comments as prose
  prose-off: (no blocks); no folds, checked=false
  prose-on: doc-1@1 markdown, doc-5@5 markdown, doc-10@10 markdown; folds 1-3, 5-6, checked=true
a theme change rebuilds the editor, and the prose is sent to the new one
  theme-set: doc-1@1 markdown, doc-5@5 markdown, doc-10@10 markdown; folds 1-3, 5-6
  the text is untouched: true
